2 CONT I6I ridsson, 1 who is named between the years 1286 and 1307, should be reason to investigate, if no kinship between them can be demonstrated. As children of Bengt Hafridsson or his widow Margareta are mentioned in separate letters
2 CONC  Folke, Ramfrid, g. roses. 2 Of these, Ramfrid Bengtsdotter lived the longest and in her last will of the year she mentions as a cousin Mr. Folke Knutsson, domprost in Skara, who is also mentioned among her heirs, Magnus Gregersso
2 CONC n and Algot Bengtsson. Folke Knutsson was the son of Mrs. Ramfrid's sister Kristina. Magnus Gregersson was the son of the knight Greger Magnusson (2 slanted beams) and Birgitta Brynjulfsdotter (lion) a daughter of Brynjulf ​​Bengt
2 CONC sson and thus aunt of Duke Bengt Algotsson (lion). Algot Bengtsson was a lawyer in Vester-, götland, carried a grip head in the weapon and was the grandson of the well-known lawyer Algot Brynjulfsson. That he too was related to Du
2 CONC ke Bengt's ancestors appears from a letter issued in 1322 by Mrs. Ingegärd Svantepolksdotter on Händelö, 4 in which he and Greger Magnusson (2 slanted beams) and Mrs. Ingegärd's sons Knut and Algot Brynjulfsson (lions) are mention
2 CONC ed as seals. For the relationship between Mrs. Ramfrid Bengtsdotter herself and Brynjulf ​​Bengtsson's children further speaks the fact that Mr. Gregers Magnusson (2 slanted beams) and Knut and Algot Brynjulfssöner sealed (1332) a
2 CONC  letter issued by her.5 Then thus both Bengt Hafridsson and Duke Bengt Algotsson and his ancestral lineage in the arms carry a lion, as they are both most closely tied to Vestergötland, furthermore Bengt Hafridsson's daughter Mrs.
2 CONC  Ramfrid Bengtsdotter and Duke Bengts father have common relatives and then finally Mrs. Ramfrid herself seems to be related to Duke Bengts father, it seems to me most likely that Duke Bengts grandfather Brynjulf ​​Bengtsson was a
2 CONC  son of Vestgöta-lagmannen Bengt Hafridsson and older brother of Mrs. Ramfrid Bengtsdotter. Concerning Bengt Hafridsson's and Bengt Algotsson's family connections in general, I refer to an essay by me in Sv. Historisk tidskrift p.
