1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Arvid Gustavsson (Sparre av Vik)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Gustav Arvidsson (Sparre av Vik) and Kristina Petersdotter (Tre Rutor) 
2 CONT * Arvid Gustavsson, Lord of Vik (died c. 1379/1380) was a medieval Swedish magnate and justiciar of Finland. His principal seat was his manor of Vik in Balingsta, Uppland. Through his paternal grandmother Ramborg Israelsdotter And
2 CONC , younger Arvid descended from the And family. His grandfather Arvid Gustavsson had the same name and coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_av_Vik#TAB_3 '''Arvid Gustavsson (Sparre av Vik)'''] son of Gustav Arvidsson. Appears at the earliest in 1356. Mentioned as national council from 1362 and as a layman in Finland from 13
2 CONC 66. Became knight in 1372 or 1373. Appears as governor of Lagunda hd in Uppland 1377-1388. Died in 1379 or 1380. '''Married at the latest in 1369 to Helena Magnusdotter,''' who probably lived still in 1373 but was dead in 1380, da
2 CONC ughter of the knight and the national council Magnus Gislason ( Sparre of Aspnäs ) and Birgitta Knutsdotter (family of the Algots sons ).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Margaret Arvidsdotter,''' Owned Vik. Died 9.4 1415 and buried with her husband in Vadstena. Married no later than 1385 with the knight, the national council and the magistrate of Uppland Ture Bengtsson ( Bielke ), who died on
2 CONC  20 November 1414 and buried in Vadstena 14.1 1415. Their descendants inherited both Vik and Örby
2 CONT
2 CONT == Swedish Diplomatariums National Archives of of Medieval Letters
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=gustavsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=18&postid=sdhk_2650&tab=post#tab 13008]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1385 December 31, of Issue: Nykoping
2 CONT
2 CONT Bo Jonsson, drots, Sten Bengtsson, knight and marshal, and Karl Ulfsson, knight and lawman in Uppland , report as executor of '''Mr. Arvid Gustavsson's (Sparre av Vik)''' wills, Mr. Anbjörn Larsson to probation at the prebend that
2 CONC  '''Arvid Gustavsson''' founded at Uppsala judgment church and to which he has allocated the following goods: land in Tibble in Husaby-Ernavi (now Husby-Långhundra) parish, in Väsby in Vallentuna parish etc. On the reverse: N vj (
2 CONC Uppsala cathedral box sign); 58 (Rasmus Ludvigsson letter sign for the cathedral) - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897410732&photo_id=6000000140355823824&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arvid_Gustavsson,_Lord_of_Vik '''Arvid Gustavsson, Lord of Vik''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Younger Arvid Gustavsson's father was Gustav Arvidsson, knight and member of the Privy Council of Sweden, justiciar of Södermanland, whose seat probably already was Vik. Arvid's mother probably (but not certainly, because some his
2 CONC tory gives him as son of a second wife of his father, of whose existence and name there are however no contemporary evidence) was Kristina Petersdotter of the tre rutor family, daughter of Birgitta Jonsdotter, possibly of the Aspe
2 CONC näs family, and certainly widow of Erengisle Näskonungsson, Lord High Constable of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT The younger Arvid Gustafsson was member of the Privy Council of Sweden from 1362, and from 1366 lawspeaker of Finland, Swedish province.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Helena Magnusdotter, daughter of Birgitta Knutsdotter of the Algotssöner family and Magnus Gislason, PC, Lord of Aspnäs, who also bore spar as his Coat of Arms, and is therefore also dubbed as "Sparre" (Sparre of Aspn
2 CONC äs) in genealogies. Magnus Gislason's line and Gustav/Arvid line may well have been of the same origin, but there exists no evidence of that.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena and Arvid inherited the manor of Örby when her parents' inheritance was divided between her and her full sister (whose family received Aspnäs). Her half-sister had been the first wife of Charles Ulvsson, Lord of Tofta, thus
2 CONC  a brother-in-law of Arvid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arvid and Helena had an only surviving child, daughter Margareta Arvidsdotter (died on 9 April 1415), who became their heiress. Margareta married sir Ture Bengtsson (of the Bielke, died 20 November 1414), PC, justiciar of Uppland.
2 CONC  Their descendants inherited Vik, Örby etc., a veritable bunch of properties in Uppland, which ultimately ended to their descendants the Vasa, and its scion, the king Gustav I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justiciar Arvid died either in 1379 or 1380. His father's first name was given to his 7th-generation descendant who became Gustav I of Sweden and because of whom, the name Gustav has since remained in common names of Swedish royal
2 CONC  families.
2 CONT
