2 CONT * Carlsson, G.: Sten Turesson (Bielke) died 1431 In the swedish Biographical Dictionary (1924)
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcriptions:  Hadorph: III E 80 mf. 142; Pering Shield: E 68: reg no. 157 (Stenh.) No. 146 (Wennæs.)
2 CONT * Medieval Regest / Note:  Minutes in SDHK No. 25494 (1449 26/3, RA perg.); Minutes in SDHK No. 30700 (1480 12/4, RA paper)
2 CONT * For the letter's context and context, see H. Gillingstam, Ätterna Oxenstierna and Vasa, pp. 247 et seq., And KG. Lundholm, Sten Sture and the great men, pp. 6-12, 84 ff. If the resorts in Sollentuna herd see DMS 1: 7 s 259 f, 26
2 CONC 5ff, 269 f. If the localities in Håbo herd see DMS 1:10 s 113 f, 115 f.
2 CONT * Gillingstam, Oxenstierna and Vasa (1952), pp. 247 ff.
2 CONT * This parchment letter, which has no. 2 in Reuterholm's collection from Svidja, is missing from the lake of Sjödens. in MRA 1939 p 117 note 1; however, is recorded at. of which 1494 20/6 (no. 38, SDHK no. 33102 ), all acc. ant. b
2 CONC y Liedgren.
2 CONT * Identification of farms after C 8 in PM Liedgren I: 2.
2 CONT * cf. 1444 11/9, perg. RA (SDHK No. 24606 ); judgment letter 1480 13/4 (SDHK no 30705 , SDHK no 30706 , SDHK no 30707 , SDHK no 30708 ); Sjögren, Trolle, pp. 218 and 213 note; Kumlien, Sten Sture, pp. 84 ff and pp. 6 ff.
2 CONT * For the letter's context and context, see H. Gillingstam, Ätterna Oxenstierna and Vasa, pp. 247 et seq., And KG. * 
2 CONT * Lundholm, Sten Sture and the great men, pp. 6-12, 84 ff.
2 CONT * For the farms in Frösthult, Vittinge and Västerlövsta, see main note for the 1449 letter in DMS Uppland 1: 8 p 71.
2 CONT * Original:  or. Perg. RA 0101 
2 CONT * Sveriges historia intill tjugonde seklet, Volume 1, by Emil Hildebrand - https://books.google.com/books?id=ia8XAAAAYAAJ&pg=RA1-PA419&lpg=RA1-PA419&dq=Sten+Turesson,+till+%C3%96rby+(Bielke)&source=bl&ots=FFOZrTTGEa&sig=ACfU3U2pPB
2 CONC fSipg3fQP7Zr-vM4tNpQvh1Q&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiQytrm5qLqAhVBnp4KHZ2vDM04ChDoATABegQICBAB#v=onepage&q=Sten%20Turesson%2C%20till%20%C3%96rby%20(Bielke)&f=false
2 CONT * Profession Chief Justice, Council of Ministers, Death 1431, Band 04 (1924), page 150
2 CONT * Profession Privy Council, Death 1439, Band 26 (1987-1989), page 433
