2 CONT * owned, in addition to Ramstad, Västbro in Bro parish, etc. farms in Värmland, as well as Rynninge in Längbro parish and Näs (now Hjälmarsnäs) and four farms in Våtsta in Stora Mellösa parish, all in Närke, but sold or exchanged 
2 CONC all these farms except Ramstad and Västbro before the end of the 16th century. Lars Olofsson was ennobled by King Johan on 23 August 1589 in Reval, was still a lieutenant in 1598, but before 1602 a cavalry commander for a banner o
2 CONC f cavalry and also a court squire with Duke Carl, and died on 23 (25?) April 1606 and is buried in the Nikolai Church in Örebro, where his tombstone with his image and arms carved can be found.
