2 CONC hers received from King Erik on 12/01/1561 for the consideration in Fittja village in Lagunda district Uppsala county, which the council awarded to their mother for Örby 7 . Sealed among the nobility, King Gustaf I's will in 1560 
2 CONC and the estates' grant in 1561 (when he signed himself to Skravestad). Was present at the mustering with the savior in Östergötland in 1563 5 . Ship's chief officer. Died 1570-06-15 on the ship Engeln and buried s. å. 13/7 in Öste
2 CONC rhaninge church Stockholms län, where his shield with the Ulf weapon and signature was set up. '''Married 1560-10-21 to his sister-in-law's sister Kerstin Marboin her 1st marriage (married 2nd 1575-06-12 at Hällerstad 9 to the pre
