1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Gudmundsdotter (äldre Forstena)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Gudmund Torbjörnsson Gumsehuvud and Ragnhild Svensdotter Lilja 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Torsten Brunsson''' (son of Brun Svensson), to Forstena in Tunhems parish, Älvsborg county and Häggetorp in Dala parish, Skaraborg county. Is already mentioned (Eriksberg's archive) 1518-02-21. Sealed a Ture Jönsson'
2 CONC s (Three Roses) Gift Letter (RAP.) 1521-01-13. Was county governor in Skånings herad (Vff I h. 2 p. 58.) 1523-11-14. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svenske_nr_258 Noble Forstenas family,, Ancient breed of salvation, introduced in 1625.]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 12'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Torsten Brunsson (son of Brun Svensson, tab 6), to Forstena in Tunhem parish, Älvsborg county and Häggetorp in Dala parish, Skaraborg county. Mentioned already (Eriksberg archives) 1518-02-21. Sealed a gift deed from Ture Jönsson 
2 CONC (three roses) (RAP.) 1521-01-13. Was district governor in the district of Skåning (Vff I h. 2 p. 58.) 1523-11-14. In the castle law at Älvsborg (GIr.) 1524-10-07. Called squire (RAP.) 1525-07-25. Assistant in the king's council in
2 CONC  Skara (GIr.) 1526-03-01. Attended the Riksdag in Västerås 1527 (GIr.). Sat in court over the rebellious West Göta lords 1529-06-00. Lagman in Värmland (GIr.) 1529-08-03 and still 1534. Again in the castle council at Älvsborg 1532
2 CONC -10-07. County sheriff in Åsa district, which district rights were given to another person (GIr.) 1537-01-16. Regimental councilor in Västergötland 1540. Was again in the castle council at Älvsborg 1543-05-00 (GIr.). Sealed the Vä
2 CONC sterås inheritance association 1544. Still alive 1545-08-09, when he sat in the regimental county council that was held in Ny-Lödöse on 1545-08-09 (Peder Swart's chronicle.). He obtained through his marriage the farm Forstena, aft
2 CONC er which the family got its name. '''Married to Anna Gudmundsdotter, daughter of the district governor in Väne district Gudmund Torbjörnsson (bagghuvud), to Forstena, of the older Forstena family, and Ragnhild Svensdotter (half li
2 CONC ly).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * ''' Göran Torstensson. Sheriff,''' Göran Torstensson (son of Torsten Brunsson, tab. 12), to Forstena and Nygård in Tunhem's parish, and Rölanda in Frändefors parish, Årbol, Åttingsberg and Åttingsåker in the Färglanda parish, et
2 CONC c. (all in Älvsborg county). Sealed the nobility's declaration of approval of Gustaf I's will, etc. (Hra.) 1560-07-30 and the renewed assurance of allegiance to King Erik 1561 (Hra.). Delivered with brother-in-law Bengt Swedish's 
2 CONC assurance of allegiance to Duke Johan (Hra.) 1568-08-20. Rider champion for Västgöta riders in 1569. In the Palace Act at Gullberg 1573-05-19. Joined Dal 1576-1584 (A. Lignell. Description of Dal.). Still alive (Hra.) 1590-03-07, 
2 CONC when he signed the renewal of the stands and the declaration of the inheritance association, as well as the extension of the succession to the women's line (Hra.). Married in old age (after 1579) with his wifeElin Gudmundsdotter, 
2 CONC farmer's daughter from Börteslevs village in Väne herad.
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''His Torstensson,''' Hans Torstensson (son of Torsten Brunsson, tab 12), to Lunden in Vassenda parish, in Väne hierad and (A. Lignell. Description over Dal.) Olsängen in Färgelanda parish, and Steg in Rännelanda parish, (both
2 CONC  in Älvsborg county). Mentioned as a witness (Hildebrand, Sv. Historia.) 1558-06-16. Sealed the nobility's declaration of approval of Gustaf I's will, etc. (Hra.) 1560-07-30 and the renewed assurance of allegiance to King Erik 156
2 CONC 1 (Hra.). Mentioned among the Savior in 1563 (Hra.), But was dead in 1577 (A. Lignell. Description of Dal.). Married to Carin Söfrinsdotter, daughter of Söfrin (Severin) Kijl and Malin Ribbing. (No. 15).
2 CONT
2 CONT * ''' Lennart Torstensson Knekthövidsman. died 1564,''' Lennart Torstensson (son of Torsten Brunsson, tab. 12), to Forstena in Tunhems parish, and Restad in Naglums parish, (both in Älvsborg county). Was joined in Väne herald in 1
2 CONC 559 (GIr.). Sealed the nobility's declaration of approval of Gustaf I's will, etc. (Hra.) 1560-07-30 and the renewed assurance of allegiance to King Erik 1561 (Hra.). Chief officer at Västgöta footmen. Stupid at the siege of Bohus
2 CONC  castle 1564-02-23. Buried in Tun's Church (At I: About the descendants of Tore Pyting.) Skaraborg County. Married to her cousin's stepdaughter Margareta Andersdotter in her 1st marriage [g. Married 2: o 1573-01-06 with the govern
2 CONC or Anders Olofsson (Oxehufvud, no. 102), born 153 (7), died 1618], died 1616, daughter of the Council of Governors Anders Hansson ( Ekeblad ) and Agneta Nilsdotter (crescent).
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Christoffer Torstensson,''' The man of the castle, Christoffer Torstensson (son of Torsten Brunsson, tab 12), to Bryggum in Tunhems parish, as well as Frändöga (Fråndö) and Kylsäter in Färgelanda parish, (all in Älvsborg cou
2 CONC nty) and Ulfstorp in Sparlösa parish, Skaraborg county. Sealed the renewed allegiance to King Erik 1561 (Hra.) And the nobility's allegiance to King Johan (Hra.) 1569-01-26. Equestrian at Västgöta Equestrian 1564– 1567. Authorizat
2 CONC ion, together with others, to supervise the fortifications at Gullberg Fortress (Gff ​​VII p. 182.) 1570-05-30. Commander at Älvsborg Castle (Off VII p. 187.) 1571-06-24 - 1572-03-24. At the beginning of 1573, he was one of King E
2 CONC rik XIV's prison guards. Lived another 1586-11-04 when he was named in a register of Sweden's nobility (Hra.). Married to Brita Stake, daughter of Olof Eriksson Stakeand Cecilia Stierna .
2 CONT
2 CONT * ''' Ragnhild Torstensdotter,''' married Carl torbjörns Son at Gunnars Torp in Västra County.
2 CONT
2 CONT * ''' Gyrith Torstensdotter,''' married to Gallowglass Bengt peders son Swedish.  Bengt Svenske (son of Peder Svenske, Tab. 1. ), to Rånnum and Sjöbo. Squire. Was governor in Väne heralded in 1540. Lived in 1589, but died in 1597.
2 CONC  Married to Gyrith Torstensdotter , daughter of the regimental council Torsten Brunsson ( Forstena family no. 2 ) and Anna Gudmundsdotter (rear head) . 
2 CONT
2 CONT * ''' Gudmund Torstensson, ''' died unmarried before 1579
2 CONT
2 CONT =Adliga Forstenas gengen # 2=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Torsten Brunsson (son of Brun Svensson, tab 6), to Forstena in Tunhems Parish, Älvsborg County and Häggetorp in Dala Parish, Skaraborg County.''' Already mentioned (Eriksberg's archives.) 1518-02-21. Sealed a Ture Jönsson (thre
2 CONC e roses) gift letters (RAP.) 1521-01-13. Var District Judge in Skånings County (Vff i H. 2, P. 58.) 1523-11-14. In the castle Holidays at Älvsborg (GIr.) 1524-10-07. Called Squire (RAP.) 1525-07-25. The seat of the King's board in
2 CONC  Skara (GIr.) 1526-03-01. Attended the Riksdag in Västerås 1527 (GIr.). Sat in the right over the rebellious Västgötaherrarna 1529-06-00. Lawspeaker in Värmland (GIr.) 1529-08-03 and even 1534. Again in the castle holidays at Älvs
2 CONC borg 1532-10-07. District Judge in Åsa Hundred, which was given to another person (GIr.) 1537-01-16. Regimental Council in Västergötland 1540. Was again in the castle holidays at Älvsborg 1543-05-00 (GIr.). Sealed Västerås ' Herit
2 CONC age Association 1544. lived even 1545-08-09, when he sat in the Regimental Council that 1545-08-09 was held in Ny-Lödöse (Peder Swarts Chronicle.). He got through his married farm Forstena, after which the family received his name
2 CONC . '''Married to Anna Gudmundsdotter, daughter of Häradshövdingen in Väne hundred Gudmund torbjörns Son (Bagghuvud), to Forstena, of the elder Forstenasläkten, and Ragnhild svensdotter (half lily).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://docplayer.se/24603233-Fran-sven-byrnjulfsson-och-elin-lindormsdotter-till-lennart-torstensson.html From Sven Byrnjulfsson and Elin Lindormsdotter to Lennart Torstensson]
2 CONT
2 CONT Forstena 1 Jönsson's death: then the children changed the legacy of their parents 3. Lindorm and Margita had the sons Jöns, Sixten and Bengt as well as the daughters Ingeborg, Elin and Kristina. Everyone used the lindorm seal over
2 CONC  leaves. Jöns Lindormsson is believed to have died before February 1440, when a presumed son Lindorm Jönsson bought a farm 4. '''The farm Forstena in Väne hierad, which at the introduction of the knight's house in 1625 was given t
2 CONC he name of the family from Lindorm Jönsson's Sven Brynjulfsson family, lies between Hunneberg and the Göta River, along the road from Trollhättan to Vargön. At the beginning of the 14th century, Forstena was held by a family, whic
2 CONC h carried in the arms an unshaft seabird, later replaced by a bag (gum) head. In this older Forstenas family were the years the brothers Åke and Esger Torgersson, of whom the latter in 1418 married Ingrid Siggesdotter. Torbjörn Es
2 CONC gersson was county governor in Väne here. When his granddaughter Anna Gudmundsdotter's marriage to Torsten Brunsson (see below), Forstena moved to the later noble and in 1625 introduced the younger Forstenas family.  Lindorm Jönss
2 CONC on This younger Forstenas family originated from Jöns Abjörnsson's fourth son, the gunman Lindorm Jönsson (spar over leaves), born at the latest in 1365 and before 1400 married to Margita (Margareta) Sixtensdotter, daughter of the
2 CONC  district governor in Vartofta, inherited Sixten Martinsson. Margita died on December 23, 1407, when Lindorm chose a camp town for her and herself in Vadstena Monastery 2. On March 26, 1418, Lindorm Sixten Lindormsson was also the
2 CONC  leader among the brothers.''' He was church pastor in Tingvalla (where Karlstad was founded) and in 1436 was also called prost in all of Värmland. After Lindorm's death, Sixten appears to be the head of the family. There is no in
2 CONC dication of marriage, which is why Helge and Tyrgil's Sons of Sons, Annan Sixth. In March 1344, Sixten and his cousins ​​confirmed his deceased uncle Magnus's gifts to Vadstena Monastery 5. After that, Sixten is no longer mentione
2 CONC d. Bengt Lindormsson. If he is only known that he participated in the succession after his parents Ingeborg Lindormsdotter pledged a farm 6 in Vallerstad, Kärda sn, Östbo heredit, in 1442, apparently widowed after his end knew hus
2 CONC band Olof Kärling, possibly belonging to the family of Sigge Djäkns brother Nils ( 64: 3). Kristina Lindormsdotter was inaugurated on January 13, 1415 to the nun in Vadstena, where the father donated, among other things. Torbjörna
2 CONC torp in Vartofta herad. Kristina passed away on March 9 Elin Lindormsdotter married (after 1418 (but before 1440) with Sven Bryn- 3 SDHK Skara 4 SDHK Vadstena 1 SAÄ II: SDHK Vadstena 5 SDHK Vadstena 6 SDHK <tonnquist.se> Page
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge in Dalarna by the name of Stig Hansson to Ornäs and Karin Olofsdotter (six-pointed star). Brun Bengtsson was a rider on the Upplandsfanan, was in 1565 wet shot at the cousin Kristoffer Torstensson's farm. Brita Bengtsdotter 
2 CONC was married to the bailiff in Dalarna, then the mayor of Västerås Nils Ingelsson. Stig Bengtsson, through his son Bengt Stigsson, was the grandfather of the brothers Carl and Nils Bengtssöner, who in 1625 was named Ulffana (no 153
2 CONC ). They had no sons, which is why the family died out. Sven Brunsson was in the service of the Swedish governor Svante Sture, who joined Eksjö hovgård 1505 and in Vadsbro 1507, and participated in the siege of Kalmar in Härhem Näm
2 CONC nd, the last walk in 1527 at the parliament in Västerås. - Married to Anna (without known family). Lindorm Brunsson to Bronäs was governor of Valla 1504, gunner and council. On 31 October 1520 participated in the Council's declara
2 CONC tion that the kingdom belonged to King Kristian II by inheritance, but is not mentioned subsequently. Married to Karin Siggesdotter, daughter of the Swedish National Council Sigge Larsson and Brita Bengtsdotter (Öra). - Children: 
2 CONC Elin Lindormsdotter (dy) was married to the castle law on Läckö Matts Kagg (). - Children: Annagm Nils Posse, Erik gm Beata Ekeblad, Brita gm Klas Ekeblad, Nils gm Brita Hard to Svanseryd, Karin gm Kristofer Ribbing, Lindorm, Elin
2 CONC  gm Peder Stake. Göran Lindormsson to Bronäs received Vilske cured in a grant in 1525, proved Västerås Parliament in 1527 but was dead before October 3 Married to Agneta Nilsdotter. Two daughters known:Annaand Ebba. Torsten Brunss
2 CONC on to Forstena and Häggetorp (known) sealed a Ture Jönsson's (three roses) gift letter in 1521, was county governor in the county of Skånings in 1523, in the palace law at Älvsborg 1525, was the gunman, a visitor in the king's boa
2 CONC rd in Skara 1526, proved in Västerås Put in court over the rebellious West Goth gentlemen in June 1529, a member of the Värmland Regiment Council in Västergötland Sealed Västerås Heritage Society Lived on August 9, 15545, when he 
2 CONC sat in a regiment county council in Ny-Lödöse.''' By Torsten Brunsson's marriage to Anna Gudmundsdotter, daughter of Gudmund Torbjörnsson (rear head of older Forstenas family) and Ragnhild Svensdotter (half lily), Forstene transit
2 CONC ioned to the younger Forstenas family. Torsten Brunsson's sons: Göran Torstensson to Forstena and Nygård, horseman, the castle law at Gullberg Sealed the nobility's assurance of assurance and Gustav I's testament Signed allegiance
2 CONC  to Erol XIV, and his brother-in-law 15 Dal Lived in 1590, when he signed the renewal of the estates by the succession association and the extension of the succession to the women's line. Married after 1579 with his wife Elin Gudm
2 CONC undsdotter. Children: Brown, Göran, Karin. Brun Göransson received King Sigismund's authority which appended to Dal. Married, had daughterAnna. Göran Göransson. Married, daughter: Elin. Karin Göransdotter, married to Per Nilsson K
2 CONC afle.'''<tonnquist.se> Page
2 CONT
