2 CONT
2 CONT Ermegård Fikkesdotter, till Sunnby i Öjas socken och Bro, (hu Brokind) f. omkr. 1445, levde 1507 men var död 1509 7/2,dotter  av väpnaren Fikke Bülow (kulor) och Hebbia Albrektsdotter Bydelsbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift i) Körning, ii) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermegard Fikkesdotter Bülow oli kylläkin Måns Bengtssonin kolmas puoliso (puoliso I Simon Körning) (28.9.1466 Göksholm), mutta ei liene voinut olla Tuve Månssonin äiti. 1466 Tuve Månsson oli jo aikamies, joka mainitaan 1564 Viipur
2 CONC issa päällystötehtävissä. (Piispa Konrad Bitzin kirje kuningas Kaarle Knuutinpojalle 9.11.1464, Diplomatarium fennicum).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Copilot Search Branding
2 CONT
2 CONT Like
2 CONT
2 CONT Dislike
2 CONT Ermegard Fickesdotter Bülow — Biography and Family
2 CONT Ermegard Fickesdotter Bülow (also spelled Fickkesdotter, Bylow, or von Bengtsson Natt och Dag) was a Swedish noblewoman born around 1445 in Göksholm, Närke, Örebro County, Sweden WikiTree+1. She was the daughter of Ficke (Vicke) B
2 CONC ylow and Hebbla Albrektsdotter Bydelsbach WikiTree+1. Her family was prominent in the region, with her father being a notable local figure and her mother from a noble lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Family
2 CONT Ermegard married Magnus (Måns) Bengtsson Natt och Dag on 28 September 1466 in Göksholm WikiTree+1. They had several children, including Margareta Månsdotter Natt och Dag, Tuve Månsson Natt och Dag, Kristina Månsdotter, and Johan M
2 CONC ånsson Natt och Dag WikiTree+1. In 1485, she remarried Jöns Knutsson (Tre Rosor), a member of the Tre Rosor family, with whom she had additional children such as Ture Jönsson Tre Rosor and Agnes Alfhild Jönsson Tre Rosor WikiTree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Property and Status
2 CONT Ermegard was a landowner and heiress, inheriting and receiving property from her first husband, including lands in Snevringe, Tuhundra, Österrekarne, and other regions www.birgerbergenholtz.se. She was known as a morgongåva (small
2 CONC holder) in Göksholm and was associated with the noble family of Natt och Dag www.birgerbergenholtz.se.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT Ermegard died before 7 February 1509 in Göksholm, Närke WikiTree+1. Records indicate she was still alive in 1507, leaving behind a significant estate in multiple counties www.birgerbergenholtz.se.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy
2 CONT Ermegard’s life spanned a period of political and social change in Sweden, and her marriages connected her to influential noble families. Her descendants continued to hold land and influence in the region, preserving her family’s 
2 CONC legacy through generations WikiTree+1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Summary: Born c. 1445 in Göksholm, Närke, Sweden, Ermegard Fickesdotter Bülow was a noblewoman, landowner, and mother of several children through two marriages. She died before 7 February 1509, leaving behind a notable estate and 
2 CONC descendants in Swedish nobility.
