2 CONT Die königlich-schwedischen Statthalter und obersten Räte [https://www.geni.com/people/Friherre-Gabriel-Oxenstierna-till-M%C3%B6rby/329660282540006121 Gabriel Kristersson Oxenstierna Freiherr auf Mörby] (Gabriell Christiernson frey
2 CONC herr tho Mörby), [https://www.geni.com/people/Hans-Bielkenstierna/6000000006421089121 Hans Klausson Bielkestierna] Ritter zu Årsta (Hanss Clawsonn rytter tho Arestadtt), Georg Fincke Ritter zu Pernå (Pernow), [https://www.geni.com
2 CONC /people/Anders/6000000008624910233 Andres Sigfridson Rålamb] (Andreas Syffridtsonn) und [https://www.geni.com/people/Hans-Bj%C3%B6rnram-till-Isn%C3%A4s/6000000007819736514 Hans Larsson (Larsens) auf Isnäs (Yfssnes)], der Silberkau
2 CONC fmann olof Knutsson (Oleff Knutzson) sowie der königlich-schwedische Münzmeister in Stockholm [https://www.geni.com/people/Jost-H%C3%B6ijer/6000000009440260238 Jost Hoyger], bekunden, dass sie auf die Klage der Revaler Gesandten [
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Johann-Pepersack/6000000014614935173 Johann Pepersack], Bürgermeister zu Reval, Johann Scdemann und Joachim Belholt (Jochim Belholdt), beide Ratsherrn ebenda, üner mangelndes Kleingeld, im Namen des abw
2 CONC esenden und in Norrköping (Nörköpingen) weilenden Königs das genau bezeichnete Gewund den Wert der neu zu prägenden Münzen - Markstücke, Ferdinge (vier zu einer revalschen Mark) und Schillinge (36 zu einer revalschen Mark) - festg
2 CONC elegt haben, die auf der einen Seite das Bildnis schwedischen Königs und seinen Titel bzw. - die Schillinge - ein E mit einer Krone tragen sollen, auf der anderen Seite das Revaler Stadtwappen.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Some sources seem unreliable.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Jost-H%C3%B6ijer/6000000009440260238#/tab/revision
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Jost-H%C3%B6ijer/6000000009440260238
2 CONT
2 CONT From Tatjaana Milla-Riikka Julin:
2 CONT Regarding the parentage of Jost Höijer, I would like to propose re-establishing the connection based on the genealogical research by Lars Bägerfeldt.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​His study provides a methodical basis for this lineage, drawing on heraldry and historical context to show the connection between the families.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​Key evidence presented in the research:
2 CONT
2 CONT ​Heraldry: The Höijer family in Sweden used the same heraldic symbols as the Counts of Hoya: the unicorn, the pelican, and the bear’s paw. This specific heraldic inheritance is a significant indicator of a biological link. ​Histor
2 CONC ical Identification: Bägerfeldt’s research identifies Count Jobst von Hoya as the same Jost Höijer who appeared in Stockholm as the Royal Mint Master under the protection of his uncle, King Gustav Vasa. This is based on the alignm
2 CONC ent of Jobst’s departure from German records and his subsequent appointment to a high-trust royal position in Sweden. ​Onomastics: The name 'Jost' was a traditional signature name for the Hoya family and serves as a strong genealo
2 CONC gical marker in the records of that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​Source Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT The detailed lineage and supporting evidence can be found in:
2 CONT
2 CONT ​Lars Bägerfeldt: 31 Jost Höijers Förfäder: från 1100-talet till 1600-talet (2009).
2 CONT
2 CONT ​The study is easily accessible for verification. You can find it by searching Google for: "31 Jost Höijers Förfäder pdf".
2 CONT
2 CONT ​I suggest we restore the link to reflect the findings of this research, ensuring the profile remains as complete as possible.
