1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jon Persson Stårck=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Per Larsson and Anna Olofsdotter (Stårck) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/St%C3%A5rck_nr_233 Adelsvapen Genealogies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Noble Family Stårck no. 233'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Knighted 1632-08-12, confirm. 1634-09-10. Introduction 1635. Family extinct on the sword side in 1973.
2 CONT The family descends on the mother's side from an old Värmland salvation family to Ramstad in Ny parish, whose oldest known member Anders Jonsson is mentioned in 1414. After Ramstad was sold by his grandson Ingemar Persson to the b
2 CONC ishop's chair in Skara in 1513, this farm was restored by another branch of the family. A member of this, Olof Larsson till Ramstad, who lived in 1555 and was married to Barbro Ingelsdotter (Roos af Hjelmsäter), had a son Lars Olo
2 CONC fsson. In addition to Ramstad Västbro, this owned Bro parish and others. farms in Värmland as well as Rynninge in Längbro parish and Näs (now Hjälmarsnäs) along with four farms in Våtsta in Stora Mellösa parish, all in Närke, but 
2 CONC sold or exchanged all these farms except Ramstad and Västbro before the end of the 16th century. Lars Olofsson was knighted by King Johan on 23 August 1589 in Reval, was still a lieutenant in 1598, but before 1602 master of the ho
2 CONC rse for a standard horseman and also a court eunuch to Duke Carl, and died on April 23 (25?) 1606 and is buried in Nikolaikyrkan in Örebro, where his tombstone with his image and coat of arms carved is found. He was childless in h
2 CONC is marriage to Estrid Olofsdotter Bååt, of an old Värmland salvation family, born 1553, died 1647. His nephews Nils and Jon Perssöner adopted the maternal uncle's coat of arms unchanged (a stork holding a snake in its beak). This 
2 CONC was then recognized by the nobility in 1632 to Jon Persson, who was then dead, and his descendants, who after the coat of arms adopted the family name Stårck, which in older times was written Sturk or Sturck. He was childless in h
2 CONC is marriage to Estrid Olofsdotter Bååt, of an old Värmland salvation family, born 1553, died 1647. His nephews Nils and Jon Perssöner adopted the maternal uncle's coat of arms unchanged (a stork holding a snake in its beak). This 
2 CONC was then recognized by the nobility in 1632 to Jon Persson, who was then dead, and his descendants, who after the coat of arms adopted the family name Stårck, which in older times was written Sturk or Sturck. He was childless in h
2 CONC is marriage to Estrid Olofsdotter Bååt, of an old Värmland salvation family, born 1553, died 1647. His nephews Nils and Jon Perssöner adopted the maternal uncle's coat of arms unchanged (a stork holding a snake in its beak). This 
2 CONC was then recognized by the nobility in 1632 to Jon Persson, who was then dead, and his descendants, who after the coat of arms adopted the family name Stårck, which in older times was written Sturk or Sturck. In 1776 the Pomerania
2 CONC n government councilor Carl Ludvig von Storck, who belonged to a German royal family, became a naturalized Swedish nobleman Stårck, under the pretext that he was a descendant of the Swedish family of that name through his great-gr
2 CONC andfather Johan Storck, born 1617, died 1683, who is said to have been chancellor in Osnabrück. This is not found in the older genealogies of the knight's house, but was later inserted as the son of the progenitor Jon Persson Står
2 CONC ck. As a kind of proof, it is stated that "Johan Jönsson Stårck is found to have signed the cession of customs freedom among the nobility in 1644". However, this is a mistake, because in the said document it says: Jon Jönsson Lind
2 CONC h (Lind af Hageby). To identify the chancellor Johan Storck with the progenitor's real son, the lieutenant of the Älvsborg regiment Jon Stårck, is hardly possible. Jon Stårck is mentioned for the last time in the regiment's rolls 
2 CONC at the muster in Vedum on January 23, 1644, but not in a list of the regiment's sick in Landskrona the same year or at the muster in Vedum on August 29, 1645. As it is highly unlikely that he burning war would have gone to Germany
2 CONC  and settled there, and there is no evidence that after the muster in 1644 he would have been transported to another regiment, one should probably take for granted the knight's house genealogy's statement that he "died in Skåne". 
2 CONC As far as we know, no proof of the relationship between the Stårck family and the German von Storck family has been provided. The last mentioned family, which at the elevation to royal status on 29 November 1753 received a complet
2 CONC ely different coat of arms from the Swedish one but not in a list of the regiment's sick in Landskrona the same year or at the muster in Vedum on 29 August 1645. Since it is highly unlikely that he would have gone to Germany and s
2 CONC ettled there in the midst of a raging war, and there is no proof because he would have been transported to another regiment after the muster in 1644, one should probably take for granted the knight's house genealogy's statement th
2 CONC at he "died in Skåne". As far as we know, no proof of the relationship between the Stårck family and the German von Storck family has been provided. The last mentioned family, which at the elevation to royal status on 29 November 
2 CONC 1753 received a completely different coat of arms from the Swedish one but not in a list of the regiment's sick in Landskrona the same year or at the muster in Vedum on 29 August 1645. Since it is highly unlikely that he would hav
2 CONC e gone to Germany and settled there in the midst of a raging war, and there is no proof because he would have been transported to another regiment after the muster in 1644, one should probably take for granted the knight's house g
2 CONC enealogy's statement that he "died in Skåne". As far as we know, no proof of the relationship between the Stårck family and the German von Storck family has been provided. The last mentioned family, which at the elevation to royal
2 CONC  status on 29 November 1753 received a completely different coat of arms from the Swedish one and there is no evidence that he would have been transported to another regiment after the muster in 1644, one may take for granted the 
2 CONC knight's house genealogy's statement that he "died in Skåne". As far as we know, no proof of the relationship between the Stårck family and the German von Storck family has been provided. The last mentioned family, which at the el
2 CONC evation to royal status on 29 November 1753 received a completely different coat of arms from the Swedish one and there is no evidence that he would have been transported to another regiment after the muster in 1644, one may take 
2 CONC for granted the knight's house genealogy's statement that he "died in Skåne". As far as we know, no proof of the relationship between the Stårck family and the German von Storck family has been provided. The last mentioned family,
2 CONC  which at the elevation to royal status on 29 November 1753 received a completely different coat of arms from the Swedish one1 - the lineage from Sweden seems not to have been known at the time - still survives in large numbers in
2 CONC  Germany, although not through the government councilor Carl Ludvig von Storck-Stårck, whose family branch died out in the last half of the 19th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =TABLE 3=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jon Persson Storck, (son of Per, Tab. 1), to Ölstorp in Österbitterna parish, Skaraborg county, etc. Chamberlain to King Carl IX 1608-06-01. Hovjunkare p. å. 7/8.''' Commander of a flotilla of four ships in Sandhamn in the summ
2 CONC er of 1609. In the castle law on the fortress of Salis in Livland, pp. 6/9. Rider master for a banner Västgöta riders 1612-04-01. District chief in Laske district 1614–1622. Participated, after the truce with Poland ended, with hi
2 CONC s banner in the war in Livonia 1617–1618. Since the war with the said country broke out again in 1621 again transferred with its flag to Livland in July of the same year. Received the same year. 22/10 in Mitau in fief under the te
2 CONC rms of Norrköping's decision for himself and descendants Ölstorp and Åsa in Österbitterna parish, Tortorp in Larv's parish and Rangeltorp in Önum's parish, all in Skaraborg county, as well as declaration of shield letter with mate
2 CONC rnal uncle's coat of arms, which, however, was not allowed to be exhibited due to his sudden illness and return home to Sweden. Witnessed the autumn session in Laske district 1622-10-23. Died "just before" June 1623.3 The feat whi
2 CONC ch, according to the knight's house genealogy, he must have performed in 1611 by driving the Danes out of Skara, which city they had already begun to set fire to, is nowhere mentioned. Incidentally, it was only in February. 1612, 
2 CONC as the Danes threatened Skara.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Kerstin Christoffersdotter (Lilliehöök),''' died around 1640 (inheritance between the children was executed in 1641), daughter of Christoffer Jöransson ( Lilliehöök af Gälared och Kolbäck ) and Christina Pedersdotter
2 CONC  ( Store ).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Per''',  Was at least from 1633 cornet at Västgöta horsemen. Died unmarried on 17/03/1637 in the German war at Sonnenburg. He appeared on February 28. 1633 at the knight's house and tried to obtain the shield letter, which th
2 CONC e father had been promised in 1621 in Mitau, but the matter was postponed. On July 3, 1634, he arrested with presentation of a. Axel Oxenstierna's recommendation for introduction, and on the 14th the council resolved that he shoul
2 CONC d enjoy salvation on his estates and be respected as a noble, until the k. m. joined the government, but the council could not assign him any badge or letter against the form of government. However, the government already issued o
2 CONC n 10 Sept. s. å. shield letter for him, which was dated 12 Aug. 1632, and on 24 Oct. In 1635, the family was introduced under number 206, which was later changed to 233.
2 CONT * '''Isak,''' born around 1611. Lieutenant Colonel. Died 1667. See Tab. 4.
2 CONT * '''Jon,''' to Rangeltorp. Lieutenant at Älvsborg's regiment. Probably died in 1644 or 1645 during the campaign in Skåne (recorded in the regiment's rolls at the muster in Vedum 1644-01-23, but not at the muster there. 08-29-1645
2 CONC ).
2 CONT * '''Anna,''' born twin, lived in 1671, but died in 1676. Married (between 1646-06-02 and 1649-09-24 to the master rider Brynte Papegoja , in his 1st marriage, born 1627, died 1694.
2 CONT * '''Maria,'''  born twin, died 1692-09-08 Entorp. Married before 1649-02-06 to lieutenant colonel Jöns Hierta , born 1619, died 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/St%C3%A5rck_nr_233#TAB_3
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon Persson Storck (översiktstab. 1, son av Per, Tab. 1), till Ölstorp i
2 CONT
2 CONT Österbitterna socken, Skaraborgs län m. m. Kammarjunkare hos konung Carl IX
2 CONT
2 CONT 1608-06-01. Hovjunkare s. å. 7/8. Befälhavare för en flottilj om fyra skepp i
2 CONT
2 CONT Sandhamn sommaren 1609. I slottsloven på fästningen Salis i Livland s. å. 6/9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ryttmästare för en fana Västgöta ryttare 1612-04-01. Häradshövding i Laske
2 CONT
2 CONT härad 1614–1622. Deltog, sedan stilleståndet med Polen utgått, med sin fana i
2 CONT
2 CONT kriget i Livland 1617–1618. Sedan kriget med nämnda land ånyo utbrutit 1621
2 CONT
2 CONT ånyo överförd med sin fana till Livland i juli s. å. Erhöll s. å. 22/10 i Mitau i
2 CONT
2 CONT förläning under Norrköpings besluts villkor för sig och efterkommande Ölstorp
2 CONT
2 CONT och Åsa i Österbitterna socken, Tortorp i Larvs socken och Rangeltorp i Önums
2 CONT
2 CONT socken, alla i Skaraborgs län, ävensom tillsägelse å sköldebrev med
2 CONT
2 CONT morbroderns vapen, vilket dock icke kom att få utställas på grund av hans
2 CONT
2 CONT iråkade sjukdom och hemresa till Sverige. Bevistade hösttinget i Laske härad
2 CONT
2 CONT 1622-10-23. Död »nyss före» juni 1623.3 Den bragd, som han enligt
2 CONT
2 CONT riddarhusgenealogien skall hava utfört 1611 genom att utdriva danskarna ur
2 CONT
2 CONT Skara, vilken stad de redan hade begynt antända, finnes ingenstädes omnämnd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det var för övrigt först i febr. 1612, som danskarna hotade Skara. Gift med
2 CONT
2 CONT Kerstin Lilliehöök, död omkr. 1640 (arvskifte mellan barnen verkställdes
2 CONT
2 CONT 1641), dotter av Christoffer Jöransson (Lilliehöök af Gälared och Kolbäck, nr
2 CONT
2 CONT 66) och Christina Pedersdotter (Store, nr 79).
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Per. Var åtminstone från 1633 kornett vid Västgöta ryttare. Stupade ogift 1637-
2 CONT
2 CONT 03-17 i tyska kriget vid Sonnenburg. Han uppträdde den 28 febr. 1633 på
2 CONT
2 CONT riddarhuset och anhöll att utfå det sköldebrev, som fadern blivit lovad 1621 i
2 CONT
2 CONT Mitau, men saken uppsköts. Den 3 juli 1634 anhöll han med framläggande av
2 CONT
2 CONT bl. a. Axel Oxenstiernas rekommendation om introduktion, och den 14 s. m.
2 CONT
2 CONT resolverade rådet, att han skulle åtnjuta frälse på sina gods och respekteras för
2 CONT
2 CONT adelsman, tills k. m:t tillträtt regeringen, men något sköldemärke eller brev
2 CONT
2 CONT kunde rådet icke emot regeringsformen tilldela honom. Dock utfärdade
2 CONT
2 CONT regeringen redan den 10 sept. s. å. sköldebrev för honom, som daterades den 12
2 CONT
2 CONT aug. 1632, och den 24 okt. 1635 introducerades ätten under nr 206, vilket sedan
2 CONT
2 CONT ändrats till 233.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isak, född omkr. 1611. Överstelöjtnant. Död 1667. Se Tab. 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jon, till Rangeltorp. Löjtnant vid Älvsborgs regemente. Död sannolikt 1644
2 CONT
2 CONT eller 1645 under fälttåget i Skåne (upptages i regementets rullor vid
2 CONT
2 CONT mönstringen i Vedum 1644-01-23, men ej vid mönstringen därst. 1645-08-29).
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna, född tvilling, levde 1671, men var död 1676. Gift (mellan 1646-06-02
2 CONT
2 CONT och 1649-09-24 med ryttmästaren Brynte Papegoja, nr 134, i hans 1:a gifte,
2 CONT
2 CONT född 1627, död 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria, född tvilling, död 1692-09-08 på Entorp i Synnerby socken, Skaraborgs
2 CONT
2 CONT län. Gift före 1649-02-06 med överstelöjtnanten Jöns Hierta, nr 121, född
2 CONT
2 CONT 1619, död 1708.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Befälhavare för en flottilj om 4 skepp i Sandhamn 1609.
