1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birgitta Petersdotter biologisk dotter till Nils Nilsson Unknown ???????
2 CONT Fadern likväl av adelsbörd ????    Patronymet tyder inte på biologiskt faderskap !
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/LBLV-JB6
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Nilsdotter-5107
2 CONT
2 CONT Britta was born in 1586 in Stockholm Sweden to parents Nils (Unknown) and Anna Bengtsdotter Gylta. Anna is a descendant of the Swedish Noble Family of Gylta. (*Gylta, a Swedish Annoint and Salvation family, whose weapon consisted 
2 CONC of a squared shield, with varying tincture. The Gylta family inherited the Hedensö manor in Näshulta, Södermanland. That manor became the Kurki (Royal Family) family's seat in Sweden. The earliest known members of this family are 
2 CONC four brothers named with the name Gylta already at the beginning of the 15th century. The brothers Gunnar Gylta (died last 1429) and Jösse Gylta carried out a succession in Kind härad (Älvsborg County) after their brothers Björn G
2 CONC ylta and Magnus Gylta (both of whom lived until at least 1412). Gunnar Gylta's son Bengt Gylta (b. c. 1400, still lived in 1480) was a lawman in Västergötland and privy councillor. His son was Peder Bengtsson (on a few occasions c
2 CONC alled Peder Gylta) to Påtorp (d. 1527), county chief in Skånings härad (Skaraborg county). The son of his was Bengt Gylta, who according to an uncertain information executed during stockholm's carnage in 1520, privy councillor and
2 CONC  lawman in Närke, later in Tiohärad. His sons were lawman Bengt Gylta and chronicler and diplomat Jöran Gylta.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Britta married Pers (Peder) Persson Stille II in 1606. They had seven children together: Anna Petersdotter Stille (1605-1703), Margaret Petersdotter Stille (1607-1687), Olaf Persson “of Penningby and Humlo” Stille (1610-1684), And
2 CONC ers Persson Stille (1611-?), Axel Persson Stille (1612-1683), Kerstin Petersdotter Stille (1613-1687), and Johan Persson Stille 1615-1672).
2 CONT Excerpted Notations re: Biography of Pers Persson Stille II: “The name Stilley is a Swedish name that is the Anglicized version of the name Stille. Pers Stille was born circa 1584 in Sweden. He died circa 1631-1635 at the Humblo F
2 CONC arm, in Roslagen, Sweden. His wife's name was Britta and they had at least five children: Axel, Anna, Johan, Kerstin, and Olaf/Olof. He and his family lived on the island of Solo, in Roslagen, Sweden. Pers was the supervisor of th
2 CONC e Penningby estate in Sweden and when he retired in about 1627, he was given a farm on the island of Humblo, Sweden. Pers died there in about the 1630's. Pers married Britta. They had the following children: 1. Olaf/Olof Persson S
2 CONC tille, 2. Kerstin Stille, 3. Johan Stille, 4. Anna Stille, 5. Axel Stille”......excerpted
2 CONT Britta passed away in 1646.
