2 CONT
2 CONT     * Catharina i Wilhelmina Stålberg, Anteckningar om svenska qvinnor (1864)
2 CONT
2 CONT Externa länkar [redigera]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Historiesajten.se om Katarina
2 CONT
2 CONT Sidan ändrades senast den 15 maj 2010 kl. 12.39
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Levde:  1584 - 1638  (54 år) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Titel: Grevinna på Stegeborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mor till Karl X Gustav och halvsyster till Gustav II Adolf. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Katarina Karlsdotter Vasa föddes den 10 november 1584 i Nyköping som dotter till Karl IX (34) och Maria av Pfalz (23). När Katarina var fyra (1589) dog hennes mor och Katarinas uppfostran sköttes sedan under hennes fars tillsyn p
2 CONC å Gripsholms slott. Åtta år gammal fick hon en styvmor när hennes far gifte om sig med den då nittonåriga Kristina av Holstein-Gottorp, och med tiden fick Katarina fyra halvsyskon, däribland Gustav II Adolf.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det sägs att Katarina var en lycklig förening av faderns kraft och klokhet med moderns milda ödmjukhet. Hon hade ett mycket gott förhållande till sin styvmor och de skall ha kommit väldigt bra överens. Hon verkar också ha betytt m
2 CONC ycket för sina syskon under uppväxttiden vilket framgår särskilt av den hängivenhet som hennes halvbror Gustaf Adolf visade henne. Han tyckte hon var både förståndig och klok och hon var vid flera tillfällen hans närmaste förtrogn
2 CONC a och rådgivare.
2 CONT
2 CONT Den 11 juni 1615, blev hon bortgift med pfalzgreven Johan Kasimir av Pfalz-Zweibrücken (26). De stannade efter giftermålet kvar i Sverige fram till i slutet av år 1617, då de flyttade tillbaka till Johans hem Kleeburg i Tyskland. 
2 CONC För att undkomma det trettioåriga kriget (1618-1648) återvände de 1622 till Sverige igen, där de sedan stannade för gott. Av Gustav II Adolf fick de Stegeborgs slott i Östergötland där de slog sig ner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Med sin man Johan Kasimir fick Katarina barnen:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Kristina Magdalena av Pfalz 1616-1660
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Johan Wolfgang Karl av Pfalz 1618-1621 (död 3 år)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Emilia Elisabet av Pfalz 1619-1628 (död 9 år)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Karl X Gustav 1622-1660
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Maria Eufrosyne av Pfalz 1625-1687
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) Eleonora Katarina av Pfalz 1626-1692
2 CONT
2 CONT 7) Kristina av Pfalz 1628-1629 (död 1 år)
2 CONT
2 CONT 8) Adolf Johan av Pfalz 1629-1689
2 CONT
2 CONT Katarina fick också förtroendet att ta hand om vården av den blivande drottningen, Kristina. Förmyndarregeringen ansåg inte att Kristinas mor, Maria Eleonora, var lämplig att uppfostra en framtida drottning, och efter att Gustav I
2 CONC I Adolf stupat vid Lützen fick Katarina vårdnaden om Kristina, förutom åren 1633-1636 då hon bodde vid sin mor. Katarina dog den 13 december 1638 i Västerås, 54 år gammal. Hennes man Johan Kasimir av Pfalz-Zweibrücken levde till 1
2 CONC 652 då han dog 63 år gammal på Stegeborgs slott. Bilden på Stegeborgs slott är tagen från Suecia Antiqua et Hodierna av Erik Dahlbergh.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravplats: Strängnäs domkyrka  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://images.google.se/imgres?imgurl=http://www.historiesajten.se/fotobig/402.jpg&imgrefurl=http://www.historiesajten.se/visainfo.asp%3Fid%3D402&usg=__FWDz9BHUfy9EaSXGaI4VTNven6c=&h=200&w=150&sz=10&hl=sv&start=1&tbnid=pCbxMlxFsbK
2 CONC 54M:&tbnh=104&tbnw=78&prev=/images%3Fq%3DKatarina%2BVasa%2B1584%26hl%3Dsv
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Catherine of Sweden (Prinsessan Katarina) (10 November 1584 – 13 December 1638) was the daughter of Charles IX of Sweden and his first wife Maria of Palatinate-Simmern. Catharina was periodically the foster-mother of Quee
2 CONC n Christina. Katarina kyrka in Stockholm is named after her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina's personality was described as a : happy union of her father's power and wisdom and her mother's soft humility. Her mother died in 1589 and her father remarried. She was a good friend to her stepmother, with whom she got
2 CONC  along very well, and are believed to have been close to her half-siblings, especially her half-brother, the king, who is noted to have been very affectionate toward her. Her father became regent in 1595 and was crowned king in 16
2 CONC 07, and her brother became king in 1611. Her brother found her sensible and wise, and she is reported to have acted as his confidante and advisor on several occasions. On 11 June 1615, she married count palatine John Casimir of Pa
2 CONC latinate-Zweibrücken. They remained in Sweden until 1617, when they left for her spouse's estate in Germany. The lived in Germany for five years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1622, her brother the king felt concerned for them at the outbreak of the Thirty Years' War and asked them to return to Sweden. The accepted the offer and were given Stegeborg Palace in Östergötland as their residence. She was 
2 CONC styled Countess of Stegeborg. Catharina was given charge of Princess Christina when the queen followed the king to Germany and during her stay there in 1631-1633. After her brother's death, Catharina acted as a foster-mother to th
2 CONC e young Queen Christina of Sweden after Christina's mother was deemed an unsuitable guardian. Catharina had formal custody of Christina in 1631-33 and in 1636-38, years described by Christina as happy.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 June 1615, she married count palatine John Casimir of Palatinate-Zweibrücken. Five of their children survived infancy:
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina Magdalena (1616–1662); married Frederick VI, Margrave of Baden-Durlach. King Adolf Frederick of Sweden was her great-grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT King Charles X Gustav of Sweden (1622–1660)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Eufrosyne (1625–1687); married Count Magnus Gabriel De la Gardie
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonora Catherine (1626–1692); married Frederick, Landgrave of Hesse-Eschwege, and mother of Juliana of Hesse-Eschwege.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf John (1629–1689)
2 CONT
2 CONT All kings of Sweden following her son, except three (Frederick I, Oscar I and Charles XIV John), have descended from her. Frederick I and Oscar I were married to her descendants, Charles XIV John was the adopted son of her descend
2 CONC ant Charles XIII.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Princess Catherine of Sweden (Prinsessan Katarina) (10 November 1584 – 13 December 1638) was the daughter of Charles IX of Sweden and his first wife Maria of Palatinate-Simmern. Catharina was periodically the foster-mother of Quee
2 CONC n Christina. Katarina kyrka in Stockholm is named after her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina was described as a happy mixture of her father's power and wisdom and her mother's soft humidity. She was a good friend to her stepmother, with whom she got along very well, and is believed to have been important to her 
2 CONC half-siblings; especially her halfbrother the king, is noted to have been very affectionate towards her; he found her sensible and wise and she is reported to have acted as his confidante and advisor on several occasions. On 11 Ju
2 CONC ne 1615, she married count palatine John Casimir of Palatinate-Zweibrücken. They remained in Sweden until 1617, when they moved to Germany. In 1622, her brother the king became worried about them, as the Thirty Years' War had brok
2 CONC en out, and asked them to come to Sweden, and they did, where they were given Stegeborg Palace as their residence. She was given charge of Princess Christina when the queen followed the king to Germany and during her stay there 16
2 CONC 31-1633. She acted as a foster-mother to the small Queen Christina of Sweden after her brother's death, when Christina's mother was deemed to be unsuitable as a guardian, and had custody of Christina in 1631-33 and 1636-38, years 
2 CONC described as happy for Christina.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 June 1615, she married count palatine John Casimir of Palatinate-Zweibrücken. Five of their children survived infancy:
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina Magdalena (1616–1662); married Frederick VI, Margrave of Baden-Durlach. King Adolf Frederick of Sweden was her great-grandson 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Charles X Gustav of Sweden (1622–1660) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Eufrosyne (1625–1687); married Count Magnus Gabriel De la Gardie 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonora Catherine (1626–1692); married Frederick, Landgrave of Hesse-Eschwege, and mother of Juliana of Hesse-Eschwege. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf John (1629–1689) 
