1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/195537193/john-hope Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 22 2025, 5:39:21 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==changes to be made by a curator==
2 CONT * Title: '''Sir
2 CONT * Name/Display Name: '''Sir John Hope, 2nd Baronet Hope of Craighall
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT From [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/488/mode/2up ''The Scots peerage'', Vol. IV, page 489]:
2 CONT
2 CONT ><strong>Sir John of Craighall</strong>, following his father's profession, and was knighted and admitted an ordinary Lord of Session, taking his seat on the Bench 27 July 1632. He was, in May 1652, one of Cromwell's Committee of 
2 CONC Justice, and for some time President thereof. He died at Edinburgh 28 April 1654, having married, in or before 1632, Margaret, daughter of Sir Archibald Murray of Blackbarony, Bart. By her, who died in childbed 3 October 1641, he 
2 CONC had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Baronet Hope of Craighall
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord of Session as Lord Craighall
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * ''[https://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]''; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 289
2 CONT * ''Complete baronetage''; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; [https://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n361/mode/2up Vol. II; page 343]
2 CONT
