1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR THOMAS HOPE OF KERSE and Feuar of Wester Grantoun ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Advocate; H. M. Justice General of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT HOPE
2 CONT THOMAS
2 CONT THOMAS HOPE/
2 CONT M
2 CONT 05/08/1606
2 CONT 685 / 1
2 CONT 10 / 306
2 CONT Edinburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 January 1631: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland by which King Charles I confirms that he has given a new grant of various lands to Alexander, Lord Sypnie. The lands in question included lands in the barony of M
2 CONC egill, in the sheriffdom of Perth, which had previously been resigned by Anna Rae, Elspet Rae, and Helen Rae, lawful daughters of the deceased Adam Rae of Pitsindie, with the consent of their respective spouses, viz. John Carstair
2 CONC s, inhabitant of Edinburgh, husband of Anna Rae, John Haliburton of Mairtene, junior, husband of Elspet Rae, and Master Thomas Hope, feuar of Wester Grantoun. husband of Helen Rae. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08sc
2 CONC ot/page/570/mode/1up RMS, 1620-33: charter number 1697]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 December 1641: Copy warrant for commission under testimony of the great seal, nominating Sir Thomas Hope of Kerse, HM Justice General, Mr Alexander Colvill of Blair and Mr James Robertoun, advocate, as HM Justice Deputes, and
2 CONC  failing them, those they depute, and others including Sir Robert Campbell of Glenorchie and others for shire of Perth, to hold courts and try those brought before them. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/deta
2 CONC ils.aspx?reference=GD112%2f56%2f20&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+hope+of+kerse&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference 
2 CONC GD112/56/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1643: Signature of the lands of Airth granted to Sir Thomas Hope and Thomas Hope. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f75%2f27&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+hope&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=1630&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/75/27]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1643: Crown Charter to Sir Thomas Hope of Kers and Thomas Hope, his son, of the lands of Airth and others, with relative Precept. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD37%2f134
2 CONC &st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+hope&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1630&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce family of Airth, reference GD37/134]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1620-1633. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate (H. M. Gen
2 CONC eral Register House, Edinburgh,1894), 1096 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Thomas of Kerse and Wester Granton</strong>, born 6 August 1606, admitted Advocate 17 July 1631, and was knighted by Charles I at Innerwick 16 July 1633; sat in Parliament for Clackmannan 1639-41, and for Stirlingshir
2 CONC e 1643; in 1640 was constituted colonel of the troop of Horse raised by the College of Justice to attend General Leslie as his bodyguard when he marched into England at the head of the Scottish army. In November 1641 he was raised
2 CONC  to the Bench by the King with the consent of the Estates, and was also created Justice-General. He died at Edinburgh v.p. 23 August 1643. He married, before 18 December 1630, Helen, third daughter and co-heiress of Adam Rae of Pi
2 CONC tsindie, by whom he had issue."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/490/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. IV, page 490
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
