1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Hope of Hopetoun</strong> (1614–1661), was a Scottish industrialist and politician. He was the owner of Keith Marischal."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'James Hope of Hopetoun', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 17 November 2012, 22:21 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Hope_of_Hopetoun&oldid=523566545> [accessed 23 Nov
2 CONC ember 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir James Hope of Hopetoun</strong> - Sixth son of the celebrated Sir Thomas Hope of Craighall, Lord Advocate of Charles I., by Elizabeth, daughter of John Bennet of Wallyford, was born 12th July 1614... He was admitted a
2 CONC n Ordinary Lord on the 1st June 1649, and was elected a commissioner for the county of Stirling in 1649 and 1650, and named one of the Committee of Estates... He died at Granton, on the 23rd November 1661, immediately on his landi
2 CONC ng from Holland, where he had contracted the disease then known as <em>the Flanders sickness</em>."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 321
