1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_af_Rossvik_nr_7#TAB_9 '''Christina Maria Sparre af Rossvik, till Fiskmansbo'''] i Nysätra socken Uppsala län, som hon ärft efter sin moder. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Född 1655-10-01''', död på 1690-talet'''*'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1:o''' med amiralen och amiralitetsrådet [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Uggla_nr_69 '''Claes Uggla''', ''friherre'' '''Uggla'''], född 1614, död 1676. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 2:o''' med generalmajoren [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Roos_nr_186 '''Carl Gustaf Roos af Hjelmsäter''', ''friherre'' '''Roos'''], i hans 1:a gifte, född 1655, död 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''She died after''' 1695-02-16 but prior to 1700. Given that no reference to a maternal death has been recorded, chances are she did not die immediately after 1695-02-16. The date marks the baptism of Sparre and Roos' seventh, 
2 CONC and last child, [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Roos_nr_186 '''Eva Eleonora'''] in  [https://kartor.eniro.se/s%C3%B6k/axvall-sk%C3%A4rv-sk%C3%A5lltorps-herrg%C3%A5rd Skålltorp gård] in Axvall, Skara, with Roos being located 
2 CONC there at the time with the Skaraborg Regiment. Roos was transferred to Riga less than year later from the baptism, in 1696-01-02. Roos married his second wife, of Baltic (or Ducth), and not Swedish noblesse, in 1700. By this token
2 CONC  Sparre died most likely in Riga around 1668-1669.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/C0052431_00092#?c=&m=&s=&cv=91&xywh=2767%2C1228%2C3018%2C1786 Riksarkivet]
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
