1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lars Stårck=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Nils Persson (Stårck) and Brita Pedersdotter (Roos af Hjelmsäter), till Läng 
2 CONT * Lars Storck , went abroad and in 1648 had not been questioned for twelve years.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/St%C3%A5rck_nr_233 Noble family Stårck no. 233]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nils Persson , (son of Per, Tab. 1), to Lång in Grums parish, Värmland county, for which he did military service from 1609.''' In 1612 and again in 1617, he was an ensign in Södermanland's ryttare 2 (life regiment on horseback)
2 CONC . Lieutenant there. 1618–1620 2 . Was dead in 1624 and buried in Grum's church, where his coat of arms still hung in the chancel in 1830. Married to Brita Pedersdotter , who was confirmed in 1624. on Lång, in her 1st marriage (mar
2 CONC ried 2nd to captain Nils Andersson Calmar, who fell on 1642-10-27 in the battle of Breitenfeld), died in 1635 and was buried in Grum's church, where her tombstone is still found, daughter of the bailiff at Dal Peder Knutsson Roos 
2 CONC (of Hjelmsäter, no. 51) and Cecilia Christoffersdotter (of Forstenasläkten, no. 2).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Nils Stårck,'''  dead before 1648, probably beaten in the field.
2 CONT * '''Lars Stårck,  went abroad and in 1648 had not been questioned for twelve years.'''
2 CONT * '''Cecilia Nilsdotter Stårck,''' to Lång with fl. properties in Värmland, died no later than 1662. Married in 1651 between 18/3 and 10/7 to her cousin, the horse master Ivar Bagge af Söderby , who survived her.
