2 CONT * Son of Johan Bengtsson, Lilja av Värnäs and Märta Johansdotter Ulf 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ulfsparre_nr_112 Noble HJORTÖ family or Ulfsparre no. 112 † Old Family of Salvation. Introduced 1625. Extinct 1632-10-01]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lars Tidemansson (son of Tideman Larsson,''' Tab. 2), to Forssa, now Sturefors in Vist parish, Östergötland county. Listed in King Gustaf's letter 2 1524-03-07 among the saviors in Östergötland who provided help in men and mone
2 CONC y for the train to Gotland and among the saviors liable for military service in Östergötland at the arms reviews of 1526–1530, 1534, 1535 and 1537 2 . Seated in a king's council in Linköping 1525-08-14 and in Söderköping 1533-07-0
2 CONC 9, on which latter occasion he is called savior 2 . County governor 2 in Kinda district 1525-08-22 and in Hanekind district 1529-08-24 with new power of attorney 1536-10-06, both of which district rights he held 2 1537-01-15. Sign
2 CONC ed the decision of the Västerås parliament 4 1527-06-27. Still called county governor 2 1547-06-11. Received a summons from Mr. Svante Sture about Forsa farm 2 1551-08-23. Summoned by the appointed king Erik in the castle law at S
2 CONC tegeborg 2 1555-08-12. Still alive 2 1558-10-05. He exchanged the horse's head in the coat of arms for a sea leaf. The children threw away the two sea leaves in the upper shield corners 3 and put a rising wolf as a helmet ornament
2 CONC , probably the same rising animal that appears on the helmet in the seal of their great-grandfather's uncle, the district governor Birger Jönsson. '''Married 1st to Ingeborg Bengtsdotter , on whose behalf he held Hjortö on 1525-08
2 CONC -22, 3 daughter of Bengt Jönsson Slatte till Forsa and Marina Gregersdotter 3 . Married 2nd before 1539 to Christina Persdotter 3 , daughter of Peder Carlsson and widow of Jöns Andersson in Gladhem in Östra Steneby parish 3 , Öste
2 CONC rgötland county.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''':
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Catharina Larsdotter ,''' died after 1580, when she lived in Lidhem 3. Married 1st before 1558 to Nils Joensson Bröms (no. 161). Married 2nd to Christian Johansson from Värnäs in Värna parish, Östergötland county.
2 CONT * 1. '''Christer Larsson''' . to Forsa. Sealed among the nobility King Gustaf I's will 1560-06-30 and the estates' grant 1561. Listed in the rusttjänstlengden 1562 and 1563 among the saved in Östergötland 4 . Signed the estates' a
2 CONC nnulment of the case against the accused lords in Uppsala 1567, the verdict 1569-01-25 and the nobility's declaration of allegiance to King Johan 6 s. å. 26/1. Lived in 1578 7 , but was dead in the 1580s. Both of his children sold
2 CONC  Forsa to Ture Nilsson Bielke. Married to Christina Ulfsdotter in her 2nd marriage (married 1st to the governor of Åland Olof Trottesson, of the so-called illegitimate Ekasläkten, who was ennobled by King Gustaf I, in his 3rd marr
2 CONC iage, died before 1553-05-26), 7th daughter of Ulf Knutsson ( Soop ) and Ingrid Jönsdotter ( Hård af Segerstad ).
2 CONT * 2. '''Måns Larsson , to Norrgarn''' in Bladåkers parish, Stockholm County. Was in 1583 and still in 1597 district governor in Frösåkers, Sjuhundra and Närdinghundra districts and Bro shipbuilding in Uppland: one of the unfortuna
2 CONC te judges of the royal council in Linköping in 1600. Died in 1604 and buried in Bladåkers church, where his coat of arms was erected. Married to his brother's stepdaughter Beata Olofsdotter (Musla), who owned Norrgarn, in her 1st 
2 CONC marriage (married 2nd to Velam Ruthven), died blind and at an advanced age in 1634 (lived 2/1 but died 24/3) at Eke 10 in Roslagsbro parish, Stockholm County and buried s. å. 13/12 and ordained in Ununge church 10 , daughter of th
2 CONC e governor of Åland Olof Trotteson and his 3rd wife Christina Ulfsdotter ( Soop ) [ 7 ].
2 CONT * 2. '''Ingeborg Larsdotter .''' Married to her stepmother's brother Greger Bengtsson Slatte (no. 97).
2 CONT * 2. '''Ivar Larsson''' , to Åby in Gamleby parish, Kalmar county. County sheriff in Tjust district 2 1559-08-12. Sealed among the nobility King Gustaf I's will 4 1560-06-30. Died 1580. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilja_av_V%C3%A4rn%C3%A4s Lily of Värnäs, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lilja av Värnäs or Lilja till Värnäs , is a conventional family name for a medieval savior family from Västergötland that carried a spar over half a lily in its coat of arms. [ 1 ] The family died out before Sweden's Riddarhus was
2 CONC  founded in 1625, which is why it was never introduced there as a form of nobility .
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Gjordsson is mentioned in Kinds and Vartofta districts in 1413. A daughter, Kerstin Bengtsson, married to the gunsmith Olof Christiernsson Drake from Västbo , and two of Bengt's sons are known, Krister Bengtsson and brother 
2 CONC Johan Bengtsson to Värnäs ( Värna parish in Östergötland). No children are known from Johan's son Christiern Johansson , but the last member of the family, his daughter with an unknown name, was married to the unsaved prefect of L
2 CONC ysing's district Peder Larsson Svenske (known 1527-1556), and became the progenitor of the nobility Swedish number 258 which carried the coat of arms with the spar over half a lily.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Landholdings and Large Farmers in Skärkind Parish.=
2 CONT
2 CONT By the mid-16th century there were a few farms that could be linked to a local/regional landholding. One such estate is the geographically combined estate complex owned by Christiern Johansson (Lilja of Värnäs) in 1562. He owned t
2 CONC wo farms in Frö and the adjacent single farm Stymla. Frö and Stymla are located in the northern part of the central area of ​​Skärkind parish. This estate was owned in 1543 by Christiern's father Johan Bengtsson (Lilja of Värnäs).
2 CONC 241 In 1509, the knapedrängen, i.e. a lay person, Knut Mansson in Stymla is mentioned among other knapedrängen in connection with a number of lay people joining Sten Sture's side during the siege of Kalmar Castle.4 The other knape
2 CONC drängen mentioned in the letter include Jöns Eriksson in Lövstad and Lasse in Brötjestad. Knut Mänsson's later fate is not known in more detail. Lasse in Brötjestad also did military service during the 1520s, but then disappeared 
2 CONC from the records. His estate in Brötjestad is assumed to have reverted to tax after the 1520s.243. Christiern Johansson's mother was Dordi Knutsdotter, daughter of Knut Mánsson in Stymla24 Christiern Johansson had therefore inheri
2 CONC ted the estates from his mother, who in turn had inherited the estates from Knut Mansson (Family Table 4.11) Knut Mansson was the son of Mans in Skrukeby and his wife Kristina Jönsdotter.  Kristina was in turn the daughter of Jöns
2 CONC  Eriksson in Lövstad (Lillie
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
