2 CONT * Elin Jakobsdotter (Bååtätten), Nr. 3, [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=321297154720002306&photo_id=6000000085090079897&position=5 '''born in 1578 in Lång, Grums, Värmlands län, Värmland & died in 1643 
2 CONC in Säter, Eskilsäter, Värmland, Sweden, per Eskilsäter Church, in Värmland Funeral Banner Family board for Lennart Silfversvärd, who is  Elin’s daughter Brita Lennartsdotter Svenske husband Lennart Silfversvärd.'''] Here’s proof t
2 CONC hat Elin was the daughter of Jakob Jacobsson Snakenborg from a couple of sources. Elin Jakobsdotter's (Baat) exchange of goods with Carl Bonde. Elin Boat used her son-in-laws Carl Jönsson Pig Head Seal. FileEngsöarkivet. (RA / 720
2 CONC 260), Created by Sweden’s National Archives. Year and number: 1633 Register: Letter writer register - T. Elin was also an heir of her aunt Margareta Persdotter, who died childless in Bro around 1629 and [https://start.varmlandsrot
2 CONC ter.se/varmlandsanor/artiklar/1999_1/ '''Elin is listed as Elin Jacobsdotter Snakeborg Bååt, wife of master rider Lennart Persson Svenske, was registered as the nearest heir.''']. Elin was around 2 years old when her mother Holmfr
2 CONC id Pedersdotter Pik married her second husband Jakob Jonsson, i Lång, Grums,''' in 1580.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =EÄ I: 699b, Adl Family Boat No. 3. Tab 19=
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakob Jakobsson Snakenborg (Boat) to Stävlö in Åby sn (Kalm), d 1627 7/3. G 1607 (morning gift 28/4) He was not, as Elgenstierna states, married 1st with "Holmfrid Persdotter Pik". See also Kjell Magnell's essay "Pelle in Ramstad,
2 CONC  Stårckarna and Elin Jakobsdotter" in Släkt och Hävd no. 2-3 / 1965, pp. 397-420.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have considered it imperative to once again draw attention to this, since the erroneous statement that Lennart Svenskes wife Elin Jakobsdotter should have belonged to the family Bååt, reappeared in the Finnish-Swedish journal Ge
2 CONC nealogist no. 2/1999. As Magnell has shown, she was the daughter of the unruly rider Jakob Jonsson to Lång in Grums sn (Värml) and Holmfrid Persdotter of the Ramstad family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pontus Möller, Nybodagatan 5, 1 tr, 171 42 Solna.
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://start.varmlandsrotter.se/varmlandsanor/artiklar/1999_1/ Varmlandsrotter A Major Property Owner in Värmland and Dalsland]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta Persdotter, sister of Holmfrid was a Large landowner in Värmland and Dalsland. She inherited salvation property in Steneby parish on Dal after her mother Karin Andersdotter. After the death of her father Per Larsson's "L
2 CONC ittle Per", she also inherited the farm estate Bro in Värmland, where she and her husband Nils Månsson Roos are believed to have lived from 1579. After the death of her husband in 1603, Margareta ruled and placed her own domains a
2 CONC lone. Only in Steneby under the Dingelvik farm she had 12 saviors. It was not only in Steneby that she owned properties. According to a protocol from 1619, she owned the entire Sund's farm in the parish of Nössemarks on Dal as wel
2 CONC l as several salvation homes in Värmland. Margareta Persdotter died childless in Bro around 1629 and as the closest heir, Elin Jacobsdotter of rider champion Lennart Persson Svenske.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a protocol from 1619, the entire Sunds farm was owned by Margareta Pedersdotter on Bro. She was probably married to a Pär Nilsson in Bro. He then owned Bro's farm and several other homes in Värmland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Already in this quote I see an error. Margareta was not married to Pär Nilsson but to Nils Månsson Roos. In addition, Margareta died childless and had no breast wings.
2 CONT
2 CONT The next quote reads: Pär Nilsson and Maret Nilsdotter were probably full siblings. Maret inherited his mother's ownership in Sund and had it until 1623.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1623, Maret Nilsdotter sold his ownership to Björn Nilsson in Sund. I believe that this heritage castle was sold within the family and can reasonably assume that Björn was the brother of Maret and Pär.
2 CONT
2 CONT If I can believe without having any evidence, then Maret, Pär and Björn were children of Nils Månsson Roos in a previous marriage and in this way Maret and Björn may have inherited the property in Sund in Nössemark while Nils inhe
2 CONC rited in Bro. For several years I have tried to clarify this for several years, but each time I have to give up. Maybe someone can help me figure this out, I'm grateful to have a relationship with both Margareta Persdotter and Mar
2 CONC et Nilsdotter and Björn Nilsson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=10286 Lillie Family, by The Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume 23 (1980-1981), page 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lillie, salvation family, whose members for a long time only used first names and patronymics, and only around SEK 1580 can be proven to have adopted a family name after their coat of arms with three lilies. At Riddarhuset, it was
2 CONC  called L af Ökna to distinguish it from other families L. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family's oldest known ancestor was the squire Lasse Ödhinsson (not "Öndersson"; t earliest 1466) at Ökna in Flöda, Söd, who first appears in 1425, when he was awarded land in Västra Okna as an inheritance from his grandmother.
2 CONC  The family tree information about his ancestors has not been able to be verified and is partly due to name combinations with people who in fact lived later than L. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son the armsman Anders Laurensson (d at the earliest in 1491) on Ökna was married to a niece of the judge at Kopparberget Knut Jönsson (Svinhuvud ) father of Axel Andersson(d about SEK 1546). This is mentioned as early as 1499
2 CONC  (Wieselgren) and appears in STb 1519 together with Sten Sture dyo 1520 together with his widow's followers. He became a lawman in Västmanland and Dalarna at the latest in 1523, a few days before Gustav I's ascension to the throne
2 CONC , then a councilor and between 1528 and 1530 a lawman in Uppland. A participated in the Västerås Riksdag in 1527, sat in the courts over Knut Mikaelsson (bd 21) in 1526, Peder Jakobsson (Sunnanväder) in 1527, the lords of Västgöta
2 CONC  in 1529 o the leader of the clock rebellion in 1534 o was in the autumn of 1540 among the Swedish representatives at the meeting with the Danes in Kalmar. His seat was Länna in Almunge, Upps, which he received as a fief in 1523. 
2 CONC As a fief, A also had Vendels and Tegelsmora parishes, Upps, from 1526 and still in 1529, in the 1530s Almunge parish and from 1537 Västlands and Hållnäs parishes, Upps,
2 CONT
2 CONT A's brother the Riksrådet o lawman Knut Andersson (L 1) was the father of the Riksrådet o lawman Knut Knutsson or Knut L (L 2), o grandfather of Helena Snakenborg , who was married to King Henry VIII of England's brother-in-law Wi
2 CONC lliam Parr, Marquess of Northampton. The family died out on the male side with L 2's son Knut L (d between 1628 and 1636) in Ökna. However, according to information only discovered in the middle of the 18th century, he must have h
2 CONC ad a sister named Anna L, who was King Gustav I's granddaughter Duke Gustavs of Saxony-Engern-Westphalia frilla and with him became the progenitor of the Rutencrantz family.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =[https://archive.org/details/historisktgeogra02stoc/historisktgeogra02stoc/page/110/mode/2up?q=Karin Historical-geographical and statistical dictionary of Sweden]
2 CONT
