1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L5J3-WWK?completedMergeDuplicateId=GXJ4-8KK
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Name
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Petersdotter-710
2 CONT
2 CONT "Nothing is yet known about Lom's personal history prior to 1641. As he came to America with the Stille brothers (Olof and Axel) it is probably that he was also from Roslagen. That was the reported birthplace of his eldest daughte
2 CONC r. The name of his wife is not found in any surviving record. Based on Swedish naming patterns, her name was probably Anna Petersdotter and it seems likely that she was the sister of Olof and Axel Stille, sons of Peter Stille of R
2 CONC oslagen... It is unknown when Lom's wife died. However, she was the mother of nine children."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT From Wayne Kuntze's Selected Families and Individuals, Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.waynekuntze.com/wk6mar201/pafn416.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 26. Måns Svensson LOM was born ABT 1580 in Sweden, and died ABT 1653 in New Sweden, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT 27. Margaret Petersdotter STILLE was born 1607 in Sweden, and died 1687 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. (Death seen as 02/13/1703; name also seen as Anna.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Petersdotter STILLE and Måns Svensson LOM are: 
2 CONT *1. i. Anna LOM. She married Gustaf DANIELSON ABT 1649. He was born ABT 1624 in Sweden, and died 1681 in Upland, Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT *2. 13. ii. Margaret LOM was born 1626 in Roslagen, Sweden, and died 12 FEB 1703 in Philadephia, Pennsylvania. She married Peter Larsson COCK 1643 in New Sweden, son of Lars PETERSSON. He was born 1610 in Bangsta, Turinge parish, 
2 CONC Stockholm, Sweden, and died 10 NOV 1687 in his island "Kipha". 
2 CONT *3. iii. Sven Månsson LOM was born ABT 1630 in Sweden, and died ABT 1685. 
2 CONT *4. iv. Catherine LOM was born ABT 1635 in near Stockholm, Sweden, and died 19 AUG 1720 in Gloria Dei, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. She married John WHEELER ABT 1651. He was born ABT 1632 in Moyamensing, Philadelphia County, Pennsy
2 CONC lvania, and died ABT 1677. She married Sven SVENSSON ABT 1659 in New Jersey, son of Sven GUNNARSSON. He was born 1632 in Sweden, and died BEF 6 OCT 1696. 
2 CONT *5. v. Beata LOM was born ABT 1646 in New Sweden, Pennsylvania, and died APR 1689. She married Lars Carlson LOCK JAN 1662 in Chester County, Pennsylvania. He was born 1604 in Sweden, and died SEP 1688 in Old Swedes Holy Trinity Ep
2 CONC iscopal Church, Wilmington, New Castle County, Delaware. 
2 CONT *6. vi. Christina LOM was born ABT 1646 in Sweden. She married Mårten GARRETTSSON ABT 1663. He was born ABT 1642, and died 1680. 
2 CONT *7. vii. Peter Månsson LOM was born ABT 1648 in Sweden, and died JAN 1677 in Cecil County, Maryland. He married Helene SVENSDOTTER 1673, daughter of Sven GUNNARSSON. She was born ABT 1652 in New Sweden, Chester County, Pennsylvani
2 CONC a. 
2 CONT *8. viii. Helena LOM was born 1650 in Sweden, and died 3 JAN 1720 in Gloucester County, New Jersey. She married Michael Nilsson LYCON 1670, son of Nils LYCON. He was born 1644 in Sweden, and died 17 APR 1703 in Gloucester County, 
2 CONC New Jersey. 
2 CONT *9. ix. Mary Anderson LOM was born ABT 1652 in Chester County, Pennsylvania, and died BEF 1701. She married John Dalbo MATTSON ABT 1671 in Chester County, Pennsylvania, son of Matts HANSSON and Elizabeth MATTSSON. He was born ABT 
2 CONC 1645 in Mantua Creek, Gloucester County, New Jersey, and died 1701 in Chester County, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nothing is yet known about Lom's personal history prior to 1641. As he came to America with the Stille brothers (Olof and Axel) it is probable that he was also from Roslagen. That was the reported birthplace of his eldest daughter
2 CONC . The name of his wife is not found in any surviving record. Based on Swedish naming patterns, her name was probably Anna Petersdotter and it seems likely that she was the sister of Olof and Axel Stille, sons of Peter Stille of Ro
2 CONC slagen.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 June 1654, after the arrival of Governor Johan Risinor "Måns Lom's widow" was listed among the "old freemen" pledging allegiance to the new governor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arriving on the Eagle with Governor Rising, was Lars Andersson Collinus, a "münster" (minister's) scribe, who soon married Måns Lom's widow. In 1664, Olof Stille's family and the Lom family (with its new father-in-law) moved to Mo
2 CONC yamensing on the Delaware River in present South Philadelphia. "Lasse" Andersson later became a justice on the Upland Court. After the creation of Pennsylvania, Lasse Andersson was "naturalized" by William Penn and joined other "a
2 CONC ntient Sweeds" in signing a deposition (for use against Lord Baltimore) establishing that the Swedes were the first permanent settlers in Delaware, which Baltimore claimed belonged to Maryland. The will of Lars Andersson Collinus,
2 CONC  dated 17 July 1689, left his Moyamensing plantation to Michael Nilsson Laican and Andrew Wheeler, who were, respectively, a son-in-law and grandson of Måns Lom.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unknown when Lom's wife died. However, she was the mother of nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT   Marriage 1 Margaret Persdotter STILLE b: 1607 in Roslagen, Länna socken, Uppland, Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Married: 1626 in Sweden 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Links Parents:  1. Per Stille  2. Brigitta  3. Per Stille & Brigitta  Spouses/Children:  Mans Svensson Lom  Margaret Lom+ Catherine Lom Catherine Lom Peter Mansson Anna Lom Beata Lom Christina Lom Sven Mannson Lom Helena Lo
2 CONC m Maria Lom Anna Petersdotter Stille 4,216,220
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternative data: Born: 1607, Roslagen, Lannasocken, Uppland, Sweden Marriage: Mans Svensson Lom Died: 1687, Philadelphia, , Pennsylvania, USA at age 80
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigrated in 1641 to New Sweden (now Pennsylvania).
2 CONT
2 CONT Aboard the "Charitas," with her husband, two pubescent daughters, and a young son.
