1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Örnflycht_nr_84#TAB_8 '''Erland Uddesson Örnflycht''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000193663924826?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000194352242840 The burgher of Norrmalm in Stockholm Peder Eriksson's wife had been unfaithful with the master rider Erland Uddesson (Örnf
2 CONC lycht), (died 1629) whose great-grandmother's great-grandfather was the miner Jöns Hansson (Svinhuvud). For this, Peder's wife had received certain gifts from the master rider, but her husband had managed to return some of it, and
2 CONC  some was demanded again after Erland's death. Whether this union resulted in any children I do not know. When the wife asked for forgiveness and repented, he took her back (Svea Hovrätt, Huvudserie, SE/RA/420422/01/E VI a 3 aa/14
2 CONC  (1641), image ID: A0068412_00073).]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Was a lieutenant''' in Uppland's ryttare (life regiment on horseback) in 1622. Horseman there. 1623 and led his company in the wars in Livonia and Prussia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Unmarried'' 1629-10-25 in Västerås by the horseman [https://www.geni.com/people/Erik-Hökeflycht/6000000067276779863 '''Erik Tuvesson Hökeflycht''''] and buried in Västerås cathedral
