1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Erik Håkansson==
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Hand to Björknäs (a farm south of Olshammar) built the church of Olshammar in 1620 and ordered a series of window glass paintings in Riga with his own and some warriors' coat of arms. On his own stained glass, he wrote: "ERiC
2 CONC H. Happened. ZV. BIERCKENES. K. M. ZV. SWEDEN. BEST ALTER. Oberst. Wachtmeister. VND. CAPITEIN. IN. RIGA. 1624. "Roger de Robelin
2 CONT
2 CONT "To Olshammar. Was a page at Duke Frans Albrekt of Mecklenburg, and under the auspices of Prince Mauritz of Nassau life guard in the Netherlands. Lieutenant at Småland's footsteps in 1615 and at the lifeguard of 1617-09-14 after h
2 CONC is brother Arvid. Captain 1618 and Commander in Uppvidinge, and so on. as well as Major 1621, Chief Commander 1622, Colonel Lieutenant at Östgöta Infantry. 1625 (CRAB). Got introd. 1625 on behalf of the nobility under number 59. A
2 CONC ppointed to the Colonel for all people in Östergötland 1628-06-14, and passed in 1631-06. to Germany, where he became head of the so-called Swedish brigade consisting of Östgöta, Jönköping and Skaraborg's jurisdiction. Death of in
2 CONC juries at the attack on Wallenstein camp at Alte West at Nuremberg. He was one of Gustav II Adolf's most excellent field superiors, and as brigadier, he took part in the battle of Breitenfeld 1631-09-07 and the transition of Lech 
2 CONC 1632-04-05. In the Gustav Adolf memorial cupboard at Lützen, which is adorned the king's chief warrior's weapon, Erik Hands is a shield mark. Even in Olshammar's chapel there are his and some warriors' coat of arms painted on glas
2 CONC s as well as in Riga in the 1620s
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.olshammarsgarden.com/birgittakyrkan.html
2 CONT
2 CONT —————————————
2 CONT
2 CONT Hand, Erik, Grandson of H 1, F in Ingolstadt 30 Aug 1632 (Restricted to St. Anna Church in Augsburg 17 Oct s). Parents: Fogden Håkan Knutsson o Virginia Eriksdtr. Page at Duke Johan Albrekt of Mecklenburg, served in the Morits of 
2 CONC the Orania Life Guard, Lieutenant at Småland's Fathers 15, Highlights in Uppvi-ting 4 Dec 16-20, Lieutenant at the Drabant Company 14th September 17, Captain 18, Major at Mansfeld's Court (Court of Law) 21 Supreme Court of Östgöta
2 CONC  National Law 26 March 25, Head of a Squadron from Östergötland, Jönköping County and Kåkind's Army 25-28, Colonel for a Field Law from Jönköping County 28, from Östergötland 29, Colonel for Östgöta Fotreg 30. - Envy.
2 CONT
2 CONT H was distinguished in the Russian war 1615 and 1 Polish war 1617-18. As a trafficking officer, he was closely linked to his fellow Gustav Adolf and accompanied this on the Freedom trip to Germany in 1620. He participated in the c
2 CONC onquest of Riga the following year and had been there for several years there; about his experiences during the field train recalls some of H ordered glass paintings in Olshammar's church.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the footsteps of Preussen 1626-27, H was in a garrison in the newly built Marienburg. After a long visit to Sweden in winter and spring 1628, when his squadron was reorganized into regiments, he returned to Preussen in the 
2 CONC summer and was now in Dirschau, where his people were soon severely decimated by diseases. He succeeded in August 1629 Johan Baner as head of his field regiment in Danziger Haupt.
2 CONT
2 CONT After half a year's organizational work with his new regimes in Östergötland and other specially assigned tasks, H arrived in the summer of 1631 to Stettin, where he joined the Gustaf Horn troops at Oder for a march to the main ar
2 CONC my at Elbe. In the battle of Breitenfeld he commanded one of the four brigades in the first match. The brigade, which was never directly contradicted, was famously honored by Horn, for "my Grossem Ardeur und Tapfer-keit" has harde
2 CONC ned in the artillery field. H's reign accompanied Gustav Adolf to Würzburg and remained there under the command of Horn, after the main army continued. In March 1632 H again joined the king's army in Kitzingen. Here he formed the 
2 CONC so-called Sv brigade, which consisted of H's regiments, the Dalregement and some relics, together around 1,200 men. During the continuation of the field, the brigade featured at the transition of Lech and the operations around Ing
2 CONC olstadt and Miinchen. It was somewhat decimated in that army when it arrived in Nuremberg in June 1632. In the violent battle that occurred between the army and Wallenstein's troops, both fortunate in fortified camps, H's brigade 
2 CONC attended the attack on Alte Veste. H was slandered on Aug. 24, captured and died shortly thereafter in prison.
2 CONT
2 CONT Om Erik Hand se https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Mobil/Artikel/12578
