1 NAME Hermann Fortunatus /von Baden zu Rodemachern/
2 GIVN Hermann Fortunatus
2 _MARNM von Baden zu Rodemachern
2 NICK Hermann Fortunat von Baden-Rodemachern
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 JAN 1595
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rastatt
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 JAN 1665
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kastellaun
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00017125&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Hermann was born on 23 January 1595, the second son of Eduard Fortunatus, Markgraf von Baden-Baden, and Maria van der Eycken, Vrouwe van Rivieren. When his father died in 1600 his cousins from the house of Baden-Durlach 
2 CONC challenged the inheritance rights of Hermann, his older brother Wilhelm and younger brother Albrecht, on the grounds that their father had married beneath his status as margrave. Their guardians Albrecht, archduke of Austria, card
2 CONC inal and archbishop of Toledo, and Salentin von Isenburg, prince-archbishop of Cologne, successfully defended their inheritance rights to the emperor. Religious affiliation may have played a role: the house of Baden-Baden was Cath
2 CONC olic, whereas that of Baden-Durlach was Protestant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermann succeeded his childless uncle Philipp III as margrave of Baden-Rodemachern, while his brother Wilhelm succeeded to the margraviate of Baden-Baden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Thirty Years War Hermann fought in Spain, then in imperial service. In June 1633 he fought in the defence of the fortress of Breisach, besieged by Otto Ludwig, Graf von Salm, Wild- und Rheingraf in Mörchingen, in which his 
2 CONC commander Ernesto Montecuccoli was killed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermann was married twice. On 18 April 1627 he married Antonie Elisabeth, Gräfin von Criechingen, widow of a Baron von Hohensax and daughter of Freiherr Christoph von Criechingen and Agnes Bayer von Boppard, heiress of Taintru. Of
2 CONC  their three children only Marie Sidonie would have progeny, marrying Philipp, Fürst von Hohenzollern-Hechingen. Antonie died in 1635, and on 29 September 1636 at Kastellaun Hermann married Marie Sidonie von Daun, Gräfin von Falke
2 CONC nstein, widow of Adam Philipp, Graf von Kronberg, and daughter of Philipp Franz von Daun, Graf von Falkenstein, and Gräfin Elisabeth zu Salm-Reifferscheidt. Of their two children, Marie Eleonore would have progeny, marrying Johann
2 CONC  Franz Desideratus, Fürst von Nassau-Siegen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hermann died in Kastellaun on 4 January 1665. His gravestone is in the Sankt Nikolaus Kirche in Rodemachern.
